# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SWARM CORE - Layer 4/5: never let git silently content-merge a CORE file.
#
# Every path on the 41-entry CORE list carries "-merge" (the merge attribute
# set to unset). git then refuses to auto-resolve any file that BOTH sides
# changed: it surfaces as a conflict that must be resolved deliberately.
# This closes the "rogue worktree push quietly overwrote a protected file"
# failure mode (2026-08-20 commit 2762682c10) that the other layers can only
# detect after the git object has already been written.
#
# Must be kept in lock-step with the CORE lists in:
#   scripts/guard/verify-core.ps1
#   scripts/guard/pre-commit.hook.sh
#   scripts/guard/apply-attrib-readonly.ps1
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.gitignore -merge
.gitattributes -merge
package.json -merge
package-lock.json -merge
prisma/schema.prisma -merge
CHANGELOG.md -merge
.github/workflows/sync-secrets.workflow.yml -merge
